GBM-allocated scan-out buffers for gamescope's DRM backend on NVIDIA (opt-in: gamescope_drm_gbm_scanout=1).
Nine commits from https://github.com/farnoy/gamescope (branch nvidia-gbm-wayland: 5cf847274, ffb525cf7, 211f4ca26,
117b593ea, 8da9459ff, cb0378edc, 4e879fbf7, 0c7fddbf3, ae7b99df3), as one diff against gamescope 3.16.31.
Upstream issue: https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope/issues/2309.
Tested on an RTX 5080 (driver 615.78.08): Steam's gaming UI is clean with it and shows artifacts without it.
Applies with `git apply` (it ignores these lines); newer gamescope versions need a rebase.

